<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan money rates ease, seen falling.</title>
<headline>Pakistan money rates ease, seen falling.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-07-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's money market rates fell on Saturday on excess liquidity and are likely to open lower after the Sunday weekend, dealers said.</p>
<p>The rates fluctuated between 7.00 and 12 percent in the morning but later rose to 12 percent, compared to Friday's 16 percent, a dealer at Standard Chartered Bank said.</p>
<p>The rates are likely to open lower on Monday because of an expected inflow of 2.5 billion rupees, he said.</p>
<p>($1 = 40.62 rupees) -- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
